      "chunkSize": 10,
      "rawToolArgs": "{\"comparisons\":[{\"requirementIndex\":0,\"lemmaName\":\"array_sum\",\"match\":true,\"discrepancy\":\"\",\"weakeningType\":\"none\",\"explanation\":\"The lemma requires equal-length arrays, ensures the output has the same length, and ensures each element is the pairwise sum. This faithfully captures 'calculate the pair-wise sum of two arrays.'\"},{\"requirementIndex\":1,\"lemmaName\":\"below_zero__ctrl_forall_to_not_exists\",\"match\":false,\"discrepancy\":\"The lemma only ensures result==true IMPLIES a negative cumulative sum exists, but does NOT ensure result==true when a negative sum exists (i.e., the implication is one-directional for result==true). The requirement says the function SHOULD return True when the balance falls below zero, meaning result must be true if and only if a negative sum exists. The lemma's ensures for result==true is a one-way implication, not a biconditional, so it does not enforce that result is set to true when the balance does fall below zero.\",\"weakeningType\":\"weakened-postcondition\",\"explanation\":\"The requirement demands result==true iff balance falls below zero. The lemma only ensures result==true => exists negative sum, but not the reverse direction (exists negative sum => result==true). This is a weakened postcondition.\"},{\"requirementIndex\":2,\"lemmaName\":\"binary_search__ctrl_contrapositive\",\"match\":true,\"discrepancy\":\"\",\"weakeningType\":\"none\",\"explanation\":\"The lemma ensures n is in [0, a.Length], all elements before n are strictly less than key, and all elements from n onward are >= key. The contrapositive clause is redundant given the other ensures but does not weaken anything. This faithfully captures the binary search specification.\"},{\"requirementIndex\":3,\"lemmaName\":\"linear_search2__C6\",\"match\":false,\"discrepancy\":\"The lemma does not ensure that a[n] == e (i.e., that the returned index actually points to the element). It only ensures n < a.Length and that no earlier element equals e. Without ensuring a[n] == e, the lemma does not guarantee the returned in...[truncated]"
    }
